    "measure": "Youth aged 15–24 who are outside employment, education and training as a percentage of the population of the same age and sex. The total comes from the published series for both sexes.",
    "interpretation": "ILO modeled estimates combine national data and modeling. The ILO Labour Force Statistics series draws on national sources and can include ILO harmonization. Country coverage, survey methods and reporting years vary. Each series retains its own values and missing years. A comparison uses the same economy, year and group.",
    "coverage": "The first and last years describe the entire series. Coverage by year counts economies with a numeric value. Each economy’s latest observed year is given separately. The raw source archive also retains economies and years with no observations.",
    "relatedMeasures": "The unemployed and people outside the labor force can be enrolled in education or training. Determining NEET status requires education and training information as well as employment status."
